          "q": "SLO SQ 1: State four major defects in Rutherford's atomic model that necessitated Bohr's theory.",
          "ans": "1. Classical Physics Applicability: Applied laws of planetary motion to charged revolving electrons.\n2. Radiative Collapse: Charged electrons should continuously radiate energy and spiral into the nucleus.\n3. Spectral Discrepancy: Predicted continuous spectra, but atoms experimentally produce discrete line spectra.\n4. Chemical Properties: Failed to explain chemical reactivity and bonding of elements."
