                  "text": "We have learnt that molecules of elements are made up of the same kind of atoms. An example is a molecule of hydrogen, made up of two hydrogen atoms and its formula is H₂. How are the two hydrogen atoms joined or bonded? Since the two atoms are identical, we do not expect one of them to transfer its electron to the other. Instead of transferring electrons, the two atoms form bonds by sharing of electrons. A covalent bond is formed when two atoms are joined together by sharing of electrons. Generally speaking, covalent bonds are formed between two non-metals elements.",
