            "q": "i. What is electron sea model of metallic bonding?",
            "ans": "The electron sea model (or electron gas model) states that in a metal lattice, metal atoms lose their valence electrons to become positively charged metal ions (kernels). These valence electrons are delocalized and move freely throughout the lattice like a 'sea' or 'cloud' of negative charge. The strong electrostatic attraction between the positive metal ions and the surrounding mobile sea of delocalized electrons constitutes the metallic bond.",
