            "q": "iii. Identify and define the four major types of chemical bonding.",
            "ans": "The four major types of chemical bonding are:\n1. Ionic Bond: The chemical bond formed by the complete transfer of one or more electrons from a metallic atom to a non-metallic atom (e.g. NaCl).\n2. Covalent Bond: The bond formed by the mutual sharing of valence electrons between two non-metallic atoms (e.g. H2, Cl2, CH4).\n3. Coordinate Covalent (Dative) Bond: A covalent bond in which the shared pair of electrons is donated by one atom only (e.g. NH4+, NH3-BCl3).\n4. Metallic Bond: The electrostatic attraction between positively charged metal ions and the mobile sea of delocalized electrons in a metallic lattice (e.g. Cu, Fe, Al).",
