          "procedure": "The first column in the table below lists some general properties of metals. Complete the second and third columns of the table.",
          "sourceUnprintedSupplementaryText": "Source prompt (the textbook provides only the first column; the name and use cells are blank): Complete the general properties, correct terminology, and practical applications table for metals.\n\nSpaceBook-authored completed key:\n1. Can be drawn into wires ── Property: Ductility ── Use: Electrical wiring (Cu, Al).\n2. Can be bent into shape ── Property: Malleability ── Use: Automobile panels, kitchen utensils.\n3. Reflect light ── Property: Metallic Luster ── Use: Mirrors and jewellery (Ag, Au).\n4. Make a ringing sound when struck ── Property: Sonority ── Use: Bells, musical instruments.\n5. Allow electricity to pass through ── Property: Electrical Conductivity ── Use: Cables and circuitry.\n6. Heavy for their volume ── Property: High Density ── Use: Ballast weights, engine blocks.\n7. Transfer heat well ── Property: Thermal Conductivity ── Use: Cooking pots, heat exchangers.",
