                  "text": "Crystalline solids are the solids in which particles (ions, atoms, or molecules) are arranged in regular three dimensional patterns. They have definite surfaces or faces. Each face has definite angle with the other face. Pure crystalline solids have sharp melting point. For example sodium chloride (NaCl), Naphthalene etc.",
