          "formula": "V1 / T1 = V2 / T2  =>  V2 = (V1 × T2) / T1",
          "solution": "1. State Charles's Law: V1 / T1 = V2 / T2\n2. Rearrange for V2: V2 = (V1 × T2) / T1\n3. Substitute values:\n   V2 = (3 dm^3 × 400 K) / 300 K\n   V2 = 1200 / 300 = 4 dm^3",
          "answer": "Final Volume (V2) = 4 dm^3",
          "problem": "If 3dm³ of air is heated from 300K to 400K at constant pressure then what is the volume of the gas at higher temperature?",
          "sourceQuestionPair": {
            "text": "If 3dm³ of air is heated from 300K to 400K at constant pressure then what is the volume of the gas at higher temperature?",
            "urdu": "اگر 3dm³ ہوا کو مستقل دباؤ پر 300K سے 400K تک گرم کریں تو زیادہ درجہ حرارت پر گیس کا حجم کیا ہوگا؟",
            "pashto": "که 3dm³ هوا په ثابت فشار کې له 300K څخه 400K ته ګرمه شي، په لوړه تودوخه کې د ګاز حجم څومره دی؟",
            "sourcePdf": "D:/SpaceBook/Books/9th/9th Chemistry/pdf/chemistry3.pdf",
            "sourcePdfPage": 32,
            "sourcePrintedPage": 132
          },
          "sourceFinalAnswerPair": {
            "text": "V₂ = 4dm³",
            "urdu": "V₂ = 4dm³",
            "pashto": "V₂ = 4dm³"
          },
          "sourcePdf": "D:/SpaceBook/Books/9th/9th Chemistry/pdf/chemistry3.pdf",
