                  "text": "Electrons are lost in oxidation and gained in reduction. Therefore, when oxidation occurs during a chemical reaction, reduction must occur simultaneously. The number of electrons lost in oxidation must equal the number of electrons gained in reduction. This name is often shortened to redox reaction.",
