                  "text": "Aluminium is the most abundant metal in the earth's crust (about 8.2% of the total metals). It is never found in free state in nature. Aluminium is reactive and will react spontaneously with water and air to form aluminium oxide. Aluminum oxide, (Al₂O₃) forms a stable passive layer. This layer is about 4nm thick and will provide corrosion protection to aluminium as long as this oxide layer is present.",
