            "q": "(viii) Why O₂ is necessary for rusting?",
            "ans": "Oxygen (O2) acts as the essential electron acceptor (oxidizing agent) at the cathodic sites during the electrochemical process of rusting. Iron cannot be oxidized continuously unless the 4 electrons liberated by iron oxidation (2Fe ──> 2Fe2+ + 4e-) are consumed. Dissolved oxygen reacts with water and these electrons (O2 + 2H2O + 4e- ──> 4OH-), completing the electrochemical redox circuit and enabling the formation of rust.",
