            "q": "(ix) Sketch the Daniel cell, labeling the cathode, anode and the direction of flow of the electrons.",
            "ans": "In the Daniell Cell:\n• Anode (Left / Negative): Zinc (Zn) rod dipped in 1.0 M ZnSO4 solution. (Oxidation: Zn ──> Zn2+ + 2e-).\n• Cathode (Right / Positive): Copper (Cu) rod dipped in 1.0 M CuSO4 solution. (Reduction: Cu2+ + 2e- ──> Cu).\n• Flow of Electrons: Electrons flow through the external metallic wire and voltmeter (reading 1.10 V) from the Zinc Anode (-) to the Copper Cathode (+).\n• Salt Bridge: Inverted U-tube containing K2SO4 in agar connects the two beakers to maintain ionic neutrality (SO4^2- migrates toward anode, K+ toward cathode).",
