              "name": "Closed-Chain (Cyclic or Ring) Compounds",
              "desc": "Closed-chain compounds contain rings of atoms joined together. They are subdivided into two main classes:\n\n1. **Homocyclic (Carbocyclic) Compounds:**\nThe ring is composed **entirely of carbon atoms** only. Further divided into:\n- **Alicyclic Compounds:** Cyclic compounds whose chemical properties resemble open-chain aliphatic hydrocarbons (contain single bonds or non-aromatic multiple bonds).\n  *Examples:* Cyclopropane ($C_3H_6$), Cyclobutane ($C_4H_8$), Cyclopentane ($C_5H_{10}$), Cyclohexane ($C_6H_{12}$).\n- **Aromatic Compounds:** Cyclic compounds that contain at least one **benzene ring ($C_6H_6$)** with alternating single and double bonds (conjugated pi-electron system) and possess characteristic pleasant aromas.\n  *Examples:* Benzene ($C_6H_6$), Toluene ($C_6H_5CH_3$), Naphthalene ($C_{10}H_8$), Phenol ($C_6H_5OH$).\n\n2. **Heterocyclic Compounds:**\nCyclic compounds where the ring contains **one or more atoms other than carbon** (heteroatoms such as Nitrogen, Oxygen, or Sulphur).\n*Examples:*\n- Pyridine ($C_5H_5N$, contains Nitrogen in a 6-membered ring)\n- Furan ($C_4H_4O$, contains Oxygen in a 5-membered ring)\n- Thiophene ($C_4H_4S$, contains Sulphur in a 5-membered ring)\n- Pyrrole ($C_4H_5N$, contains Nitrogen in a 5-membered ring)",
