              "desc": "A **functional group** is an atom or group of atoms that imparts specific, characteristic chemical properties to an organic molecule regardless of the size or structure of the attached carbon skeleton.\n\n**Major Classes of Functional Groups:**\n1. **Functional Groups Containing Oxygen:**\n   - **Alcohol (Hydroxyl group, $-OH$):** General formula $R-OH$. *Example:* Ethanol ($C_2H_5OH$), Methanol ($CH_3OH$).\n   - **Ether (Ether linkage, $-O-$):** General formula $R-O-R'$. *Example:* Diethyl ether ($C_2H_5-O-C_2H_5$), Dimethyl ether ($CH_3-O-CH_3$).\n   - **Aldehyde (Formyl group, $-CHO$):** Carbonyl bonded to at least one hydrogen: $R-CHO$. *Example:* Formaldehyde ($HCHO$), Acetaldehyde ($CH_3CHO$).\n   - **Ketone (Carbonyl group, $>C=O$):** Carbonyl bonded to two carbon radicals: $R-CO-R'$. *Example:* Acetone / Propanone ($CH_3COCH_3$).\n   - **Carboxylic Acid (Carboxyl group, $-COOH$):** General formula $R-COOH$. *Example:* Formic acid ($HCOOH$), Acetic acid ($CH_3COOH$).\n   - **Ester (Ester linkage, $-COO-$):** General formula $R-COO-R'$. Have characteristic sweet fruity smells. *Example:* Ethyl acetate ($CH_3COOC_2H_5$).\n\n2. **Functional Groups Containing Nitrogen:**\n   - **Amine (Amino group, $-NH_2$):** General formula $R-NH_2$. *Example:* Methylamine ($CH_3NH_2$).\n\n3. **Functional Groups Containing Halogens:**\n   - **Alkyl Halide (Haloalkane, $-X$ where $X = F, Cl, Br, I$):** General formula $R-X$. *Example:* Methyl chloride ($CH_3Cl$), Ethyl bromide ($C_2H_5Br$).",
