              "desc": "Hydrocarbons are the simplest organic compounds composed exclusively of carbon and hydrogen. They are classified into two major categories:\n\n1. **Open-Chain (Aliphatic) Hydrocarbons:**\n- **Saturated Hydrocarbons (Alkanes):** Hydrocarbons in which all carbon-carbon bonds are single covalent bonds ($C-C$). Every carbon atom is $sp^3$-hybridized and forms four single bonds with other atoms. General formula: $C_nH_{2n+2}$.\n- **Unsaturated Hydrocarbons:** Hydrocarbons that contain at least one multiple carbon-carbon bond:\n  - *Alkenes (Olefins):* Contain at least one carbon-carbon double bond ($C=C$). General formula: $C_nH_{2n}$.\n  - *Alkynes (Acetylenes):* Contain at least one carbon-carbon triple bond ($C\\equiv C$). General formula: $C_nH_{2n-2}$.\n\n2. **Closed-Chain (Cyclic) Hydrocarbons:**\n- **Alicyclic Hydrocarbons:** Ring structures that do not contain a benzene nucleus (e.g. Cyclopropane, Cyclohexane).\n- **Aromatic Hydrocarbons:** Ring structures containing at least one alternating conjugated benzene ring (e.g. Benzene, Toluene).",
