            "q": "2. Write down four uses of lipids.",
            "ans": "1. **Concentrated Energy Reserve:** Store long-term energy yielding $38\\text{ kJ/g}$, over double the energy of carbohydrates.\n2. **Cell Membrane Formation:** Phospholipids and cholesterol form the structural lipid bilayer of all cellular membranes.\n3. **Thermal Insulation & Cushioning:** Subcutaneous fat layers prevent heat loss in cold weather and cushion vital organs (heart, kidneys) from mechanical shocks.\n4. **Solvent for Fat-Soluble Vitamins:** Enable the biological absorption and transport of essential vitamins A, D, E, and K."
