              "desc": "**Ozone ($O_3$):** An allotropic triatomic form of oxygen, bluish in colour with a pungent odour.\n\n**Location:**\nAlthough present in small amounts throughout the atmosphere, **$90\\%$ of all ozone resides in the Stratosphere** between altitudes of **$25\\text{ km}$ and $30\\text{ km}$**, forming the **Ozone Layer** (Ozonosphere).\n\n**Photochemical Formation (Chapman Cycle):**\nOzone is generated naturally in the stratosphere when high-energy solar UV-C photons ($< 240\\text{ nm}$) photolyze molecular oxygen into free oxygen atoms (radicals):\n$O_2 \\xrightarrow{\\text{Solar UV-C}} O + O$\nThese reactive atomic oxygen radicals then combine with unbroken oxygen molecules in the presence of a third stabilizing body ($M$, such as $N_2$):\n$O + O_2 + M \\rightarrow O_3 + M$\n\n**Importance of the Ozone Shield:**\nThe stratospheric ozone layer acts as an irreplaceable planetary sunscreen. It absorbs over **$99\\%$ of lethal high-energy solar ultraviolet rays (UV-B and UV-C)**, converting UV energy harmlessly into heat:\n$O_3 \\xrightarrow{\\text{Solar UV-B}} O_2 + O$\nWithout this protective umbrella, terrestrial life could not exist.",
