              "num": "14.5.2",
              "name": "Catalytic Depletion of Ozone by Chlorofluorocarbons (CFCs)",
              "desc": "**Chlorofluorocarbons (CFCs or Freons):**\nNon-toxic, non-flammable, highly stable volatile compounds containing carbon, chlorine, and fluorine (e.g. Freon-11 $CFCl_3$, Freon-12 $CF_2Cl_2$). Developed as refrigerants, air-conditioner coolants, aerosol propellants, and plastic foam-blowing agents.\n\n**Mechanism of Catalytic Ozone Destruction:**\nBecause CFCs are chemically inert, they do not decompose in the troposphere. Over decades, they slowly diffuse upward into the mid-stratosphere. There, intense ultraviolet radiation breaks the carbon-chlorine bond, releasing **free chlorine radicals ($Cl^\\bullet$)**:\n$CFCl_3 \\xrightarrow{\\text{Solar UV}} \\dot{C}FCl_2 + Cl^\\bullet$\n\nThe atomic chlorine radical acts as an extraordinarily efficient catalyst that destroys ozone in a self-perpetuating two-step catalytic chain reaction:\n- Step 1: Chlorine radical attacks ozone to form chlorine monoxide radical and oxygen gas:\n  $Cl^\\bullet + O_3 \\rightarrow ClO^\\bullet + O_2$\n- Step 2: Chlorine monoxide radical reacts with a free oxygen atom, regenerating the original chlorine radical:\n  $ClO^\\bullet + O \\rightarrow Cl^\\bullet + O_2$\n\n**Overall Net Reaction:**\n$O_3 + O \\rightarrow 2O_2$\n**Catalytic Efficiency:** Because the chlorine radical is regenerated unchanged at the end of every cycle, **a single chlorine radical can destroy over 100,000 ozone molecules** before being scavenged!\n\n**Consequences of Ozone Depletion:**\n1. **Human Health:** Increased exposure to UV-B causes malignant melanoma skin cancer, eye cataracts, and suppressed immune systems.\n2. **Marine Life:** Destroys surface phytoplankton (the microscopic photosynthetic base of all oceanic food webs).\n3. **Crops & Materials:** Reduces agricultural crop yields of soybeans and wheat, and causes accelerated degradation of outdoor paints and plastics.",
