            "q": "2. (a) Air is polluted in big cities of Pakistan, justify the statement. (b) Enlist the main sources of air pollution. (c) Prove that oxides of nitrogen and sulphur cause air pollution. (d) Enlist the effects of air pollution.",
            "ans": "**(a) Justification:**\nMajor Pakistani metropolises (Lahore, Karachi, Faisalabad, Peshawar) routinely rank among the world's most polluted cities according to Air Quality Index (AQI) ratings. In winter, thermal inversion traps dense particulate matter (PM2.5) and emissions near ground level, producing hazardous toxic smog that impairs visibility and causes widespread respiratory emergencies.\n\n**(b) Main Sources of Air Pollution:**\n1. Emissions from poorly tuned vehicles and smoky two-stroke rickshaws burning low-grade leaded and high-sulphur fuel.\n2. Smoke and fly ash from coal-fired brick kilns and thermal power plants.\n3. Industrial emissions from steel mills, textile processing units, and chemical factories.\n4. Open burning of crop stubble in agricultural fields and municipal solid waste heaps.\n\n**(c) Proof that Oxides of Nitrogen and Sulphur Cause Pollution:**\n- **Oxides of Sulphur ($SO_x$):** Emitted from burning sulphur-containing coal and heavy furnace oil. When $SO_2$ gas reacts with atmospheric water, it oxidizes to form strong sulphuric acid: $2SO_2 + O_2 + 2H_2O \\rightarrow 2H_2SO_4$, causing devastating acid rain.\n- **Oxides of Nitrogen ($NO_x$):** High combustion temperatures in vehicle engines form $NO$ and $NO_2$. $NO_2$ reacts with sunlight and hydrocarbons to generate harmful ground-level ozone ($O_3$) and photochemical smog, and combines with moisture to form nitric acid ($HNO_3$).\n\n**(d) Effects of Air Pollution:**\n1. Severe human respiratory illnesses: chronic asthma, bronchitis, lung cancer, and eye irritation.\n2. Stone cancer and structural corrosion of buildings and bridges.\n3. Photochemical smog drastically reducing transport visibility and causing road accidents."
