            "q": "5. (a) Describe the greenhouse effect with a labelled sketch. (b) Name any four greenhouse gases. (c) What is the relationship between the greenhouse effect and global warming?",
            "ans": "**(a) Description and Sketch of Greenhouse Effect:**\nThe natural phenomenon in which greenhouse gases in the atmosphere absorb outgoing longwave infrared radiation emitted by Earth and re-radiate it back, keeping the planet warm.\n\n```text\nIncoming Solar Radiation (Short-wave visible light passes freely)\n             |      |      |\n             v      v      v\n================= ATMOSPHERE (CO2, CH4, N2O, H2O) =================\n                    ^  \\  ^  /\n    Trapped IR Heat |   v | v  (Re-radiated back to Earth)\n                    |     |\n+-------------------+-----+--------------------------------------+\n|                 EARTH'S SURFACE (Warmed)                       |\n|    Re-emits Long-wave Infrared (Thermal) Radiation             |\n+----------------------------------------------------------------+\n```\n\n**(b) Four Major Greenhouse Gases:**\n1. Carbon Dioxide ($CO_2$)\n2. Methane ($CH_4$)\n3. Nitrous Oxide ($N_2O$)\n4. Chlorofluorocarbons (CFCs)\n\n**(c) Relationship between Greenhouse Effect and Global Warming:**\n- The **Greenhouse Effect** is a natural physical process essential for sustaining life; without it, Earth would be a frozen ball at -18°C.\n- **Global Warming** is the *unnatural enhancement* of this greenhouse effect caused by excessive human emissions of $CO_2$ and other greenhouse gases from burning fossil fuels. As GHG concentrations rise, more outgoing heat is trapped, causing the average global planetary temperature to rise continuously."
